You need to see how the gismu are grouped semantically - this is
sometimes shown by the cross-references on the right, but they are not
all that systematic or clear about the relationship, i admit.

milxe, mutce, and traji are related, and deal with scales.  If you think
of one of those bidirectional scales, we have na'e'/no'e/to'e to
position on the scale.  For unidirectional scales, or close-ended
scales, milxe is akin to nutli and na'e, and is more or less neutral and
thus not towards any direction.  mutce is towards an extreme, and if
there is more than one extreme direction, you need to know which one.

carmi and denmi are contrasting in meaning - total amount vs.
concentration, and are particular kinds of scales, so you can have mutce
carmi and milxe carmi, mutce denmi, milxe denmi, etc.

